From 206fdb50610beeb6629c44c95563f54204bac3ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kalaga <kalaga@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:14:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 65/67] resource: a texture whose host copy was let go leaves
 the sweeps until used again

let_go_idle let a texture's host copy go but kept its last-use stamp,
so it stayed idle for good: every sweep over the line sorted it and took
its lock, finding nothing to let go. The longer a session ran, the more
there were and the longer each sweep took (3 ms after a minute, 14 ms
after 30 minutes in foxhound's measurements, with lag and stuttering
sound). The stamp is cleared there; the next use stamps it again under
the same lock, and the sweeps already pass stamp 0 by.

After readmet3xt-lab/foxhound 0.2.0-pre.4 (issue #12).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6tkVHCftUUQbGm5NirGaG
---
 crates/victory-gpu/src/resource.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/victory-gpu/src/resource.rs b/crates/victory-gpu/src/resource.rs
index a7473d8a..abd8a552 100644
--- a/crates/victory-gpu/src/resource.rs
+++ b/crates/victory-gpu/src/resource.rs
@@ -2240,6 +2240,13 @@ pub(crate) fn let_go_idle() {
                 // state of the texture let go (it says "uploaded").
                 crate::texture::unstage(at as This);
                 r.host.wanted.store(u32::MAX, Relaxed);
+                // Not used since: the sweeps pass it by (`used == 0`) until a
+                // use makes its copy again and stamps it, under this lock.
+                // Kept, it stayed "idle" for good and every sweep sorted it
+                // and took its lock, finding nothing to let go: the more a
+                // session had let go, the longer each sweep (3 ms a sweep
+                // after a minute, 14 ms after 30: readmet3xt-lab/foxhound #12).
+                r.host.used.store(0, Relaxed);
                 made.take()
             } else {
                 None
